doctype html
html(lang='en')
  head
    meta(charset='utf-8')
    meta(name='viewport' content='width=device-width, initial-scale=1')
    meta(name='csrf-token' content=csrfToken)
    title TARIC assisted classification
    link(rel='stylesheet' href='/css/color-theme.css')
    link(rel='stylesheet' href='/css/taric.css')
    script(src='/js/taric-admin.js' defer)
    include includes/navigation_assets
  body
    include includes/navigation
    main
      nav
        a(href='/admin/taric/codes') Approved codes and stable descriptions
        a(href='/admin') Administration
        a(href='/admin/taric/history') Request history and human review
      h1 TARIC assisted classification
      p A suggestion always needs human confirmation. Diagnostic benchmark scores, including v0 and imported drafts, cannot authorize release.
      p#status(role='status' aria-live='polite') Loading readiness…
      section
        h2 Readiness and release reasons
        button#refresh(type='button') Refresh status
        p#execution-help
        pre#readiness
        p Read status, explicitly cancel pending work, then request recovery. Recovery acquires exclusive Gateway admission without starting GPU, holds it during the database handoff, and releases only that session with verified cleanup. Busy or uncertain recovery keeps the hold. Passive status is idle_unverified, an observation rather than an error. Cleanup may continue on the server for up to 100 seconds; closing this page does not cancel it. Clearing does not resume paused runs.
        button#remote-status(type='button') Read remote status (no GPU work)
        pre#recovery-status
        p#recovery-help
        label
          input#confirm-idle(type='checkbox')
          |  I authorize pending-work cancellation / exclusive admission recovery (no inference)
        button#cancel-pending(type='button' disabled) Cancel all pending local work (keep remote hold)
        button#resume(type='button' disabled) Acquire recovery admission
      section
        h2 Dedicated integration credential
        p One active key, expiring after 90 days. Rotation immediately revokes the previous generation and queued authority. Store the new key in the caller’s secret store.
        button#rotate(type='button') Create / rotate key
        button#revoke(type='button') Revoke key
        div#secret-panel(hidden)
          p Copy now. This value is shown only once and clears from this page after 60 seconds.
          output#secret
          button#clear-secret(type='button') Clear key
      section
        h2 Configuration
        p Enabling permits explicitly requested test calls when v0 is imported. Normal mode still requires the current independent benchmark, approved catalog and verified runtime identity.
        label
          input#enabled(type='checkbox')
          |  Enable tool (clear for kill switch)
        label(for='max-tokens') Maximum output tokens (1–512)
        input#max-tokens(type='number' min='1' max='512' value='256')
        label(for='test-adapters') Test adapters (one name per line, maximum 20)
        textarea#test-adapters(rows='4' maxlength='2019' spellcheck='false' placeholder='taric-v1.1-20261007')
        p Add names already available to the inference service. Each adapter must use the current TARIC prompt and output format.
        label(for='default-test-adapter') Default test adapter
        select#default-test-adapter
        p Save configuration to apply these choices. The default is used for test requests and history reprocessing; v0 benchmark runs can use any saved test adapter.
        label(for='catalog') Approved catalog JSON (null keeps normal mode closed)
        textarea#catalog(rows='8' spellcheck='false') null
        label(for='runtime') Runtime attestations JSON; immutable identity capability is currently UNAVAILABLE
        textarea#runtime(rows='8' spellcheck='false') {"adapters":[]}
        p See the runbook for catalog and runtime field schemas. Saving invalidates earlier scores.
        button#save-config(type='button') Save configuration
      section
        h2 Test a stored AmiAmi item
        p#test-adapter-status Uses the saved default test adapter.
        p Only an item code and caller hints are accepted; facts come from AmiAmi. This action calls the provider when the tool is enabled.
        label(for='test-code') AmiAmi gcode
        input#test-code(type='text' maxlength='64')
        label(for='test-name') Descriptive category
        input#test-name(type='text' maxlength='500')
        label(for='test-hs') HS code (six digits, optionally dotted)
        input#test-hs(type='text' maxlength='7')
        button#test(type='button' disabled) Submit manual-confirmation test
        button#test-poll(type='button') Poll test
        p Generated diagnostic text is UNVALIDATED / REJECTED and cannot be applied as an approved suggestion. A test allowlist rejection is not a legal TARIC validity judgment. Historical discarded output is not captured and cannot be recovered.
        p#approval-alert(role='alert' hidden)
        pre#test-result
        label(for='test-selected-code') Human-selected final TARIC code (ten digits)
        input#test-selected-code(type='text' maxlength='10' pattern='[0-9]{10}')
        p Submit only after reviewing a terminal result or choosing a manual fallback. One final choice is immutable and remains unverified.
        button#test-feedback(type='button') Record final choice
        pre#test-feedback-result
      section#benchmark-import
        h2 Benchmark import
        p
          a(href='/admin/taric/history?review=verified#benchmark-export') Export verified history as benchmark CSV
          |  to build a first dataset with unique products and broad TARIC code coverage, ready to upload here.
        p CSV inputs: descriptive_name, full_item_name, specs, hs_code. Required target: taric_code. Optional description_summary is scored for lexical overlap only. Private rows stay in MongoDB; they are never added to the public catalog as official labels.
        input#csv(type='file' accept='.csv,text/csv')
        label(for='version') Version (0 is permanently training-derived)
        input#version(type='number' min='0' max='10000' value='0')
        label(for='review') Review and frozen scoring policy JSON
        textarea#review(rows='12' spellcheck='false') {"targetsReviewed":false,"independent":false,"trainingExcluded":false,"provenance":"Training-derived diagnostic benchmark","reviewer":"operator","sourceLineage":["v0"],"minExact":1,"maxInvalid":0}
        p Defaults describe the original v0 training data. For a new dataset, describe its actual source and review status; verified labels alone do not establish training independence. Diagnostic mode permits overlap and unreviewed declarations. The default thresholds require 100% exact codes and 0 invalid outputs; scores remain available below these thresholds. Review and choose explicitly before import; policy is immutable afterward.
        button#preview(type='button') Preview hash and validation
        button#import(type='button' disabled) Import immutable draft
        pre#import-report
      section
        h2 Benchmark execution and publication
        p Run any imported benchmark in Diagnostic mode, including v1+ drafts, without reimporting or publishing. Training overlap is allowed; scores measure this dataset and do not establish performance on unseen products. Benchmark runs make live provider calls; run them only during an authorized GPU window.
        p Diagnostic output validation uses the selected benchmark's target codes as a non-authoritative allowlist. Codes outside that list count as invalid for this evaluation; this is not a legal TARIC validity judgment. A passing diagnostic score never authorizes release or replaces the release benchmark.
        p Successful cases share one owned session. Its 120-second idle lease is renewed; its 15-minute hard cap cannot be extended. Rotation reserves 260 seconds for the next generation, reconciliation and cleanup, or occurs at 256 operations. Interactive requests take priority after the current case and cleanup; rotated runs go behind waiting benchmarks. The whole run has a six-hour deadline and can be cancelled here.
        p Saved test adapters are available for diagnostic runs without metadata calls. Release evaluation requires the current published independent v1+ benchmark, an approved catalog and verified runtime identity, which is currently unavailable. Publishing explicitly replaces the release benchmark and holds older normal results; it is not needed for diagnostics.
        p Adapter discovery is unavailable until Gateway provides a guaranteed GPU-free route; its current fallback can acquire the GPU. Add test adapter names in Configuration above.
        button#adapters(type='button') Check adapter metadata availability
        label(for='adapter') Adapter to benchmark
        select#adapter
        label(for='benchmark-id') Benchmark version (newest first)
        select#benchmark-id(disabled)
        p#benchmark-help Loading benchmark versions…
        button#benchmarks-more(type='button' disabled) Load more versions
        label(for='benchmark-mode') Evaluation mode
        select#benchmark-mode
          option(value='diagnostic' selected) Diagnostic — any imported benchmark
          option(value='release') Release qualification
        p#benchmark-mode-help
        button#run(type='button' disabled) Queue diagnostic benchmark
        button#publish(type='button' disabled) Publish this benchmark
        label(for='run-id') Run ID to cancel / revoke
        input#run-id(type='text' maxlength='32')
        button#cancel(type='button') Cancel future cases / revoke completed run
        button#run-progress(type='button') Load progress and case outputs
        pre#run-progress-output
        p The run deadline and current session expiry are visible in private run records below. Closing this page does not cancel a run; use Cancel run to stop it. Progress persists after this page closes. Errors count against the full benchmark denominator; uncertain attempts are never silently retried. Open private results below for further pages.
        label
          input#confirm-run(type='checkbox')
          |  I authorize the next cases during the current GPU window
        button#resume-run(type='button' disabled) Resume paused run after idle recovery
      section
        h2 Private inspection
        select#kind
          option(value='requests') Requests
          option(value='feedback') Feedback
          option(value='benchmarks') Benchmark versions
          option(value='runs') Runs and scores
        button#inspect(type='button') Load first page
        button#next(type='button' disabled) Next page
        pre#records
        label(for='detail-id') Benchmark or run ID for private cases/results
        input#detail-id(type='text' maxlength='32')
        label(for='offset') Case/result offset
        input#offset(type='number' min='0' max='500' step='25' value='0')
        button#detail(type='button') Show 25 cases/results
        pre#details
